{"step_index":62,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-02T21:43:43Z","thinking":"**Planning the main application structure**\n\nThe application's core file must handle these key elements. There is a need for a FastAPI application with CORS enabled. A Neo4j database session needs to be created as a dependency. Role-Based Access Control via an authentication header should also be included.\n\n\n**Clarifying Cytoscape.js data format**\n\nThe immediate focus involves structuring Neo4j graph data for Cytoscape.js. The prompt requires a specific data structure: an array of elements where each element is a dictionary with a \"data\" key containing an \"id\", \"source\", \"target\", and \"label\". This directly contrasts with standard Cytoscape.js node and edge formats.\n\nA key discrepancy emerges, as nodes in Cytoscape.js typically lack \"source\" and \"target\" attributes. The format may require explicitly including these attributes with null values for nodes, though that's not typical in Cytoscape.js. Needs clarification. The standard structure is confirmed: nodes need only `id` and edges require `source` and `target`.\n\n\n**Confirming Cytoscape.js element structure**\n\nThe core of determining nodes vs edges within Cytoscape.js centers on the presence and definition of 'source' and 'target' attributes within the \"data\" object. An edge is identified if both 'source' and 'target' exist and are defined. Conversely, an element is classified as a node when 'source' is absent or undefined.\n\nNo need to explicitly include `source: None` in the data for nodes. This format is natively compatible, where nodes have `id`, `label`, `type` and edges have `id`, `source`, `target`, and `label`. This simplifies the element creation.\n\n\n**Mapping Neo4j records to Cytoscape.js**\n\nThe Cypher query retrieves nodes and relationships; the Neo4j Python driver's results must be processed. Iterating through the records, each node and relationship is extracted. Node and edge data are assembled into the Cytoscape.js format.\n\nNodes are identified by checking `n` and `m` in each record. Each node uses its element ID or ID as the unique ID, and display labels derive from properties like \"label\", \"name\", and type is derived from labels.\n\nEdges are identified by `r` in the record. The 'source' and 'target' are found using `start_node` and `end_node` attributes of the relationship object. An edge element includes the 'source' and 'target' node IDs.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"FastAPI law enforcement intelligence platform application implementation.\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"# =====================================================================\\n# requirements.txt\\n# =====================================================================\\n# fastapi>=0.110.0\\n# uvicorn[standard]>=0.28.0\\n# neo4j>=5.18.0\\n# pydantic>=2.6.0\\n# =====================================================================\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\nimport logging\\nimport os\\nfrom typing import Any, Generator\\n\\nfrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, Header, HTTPException, status\\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\\n\\ntry:\\n    from neo4j import GraphDatabase, Driver, Session\\n    from neo4j.exceptions import ServiceUnavailable, AuthError\\n    HAS_NEO4J_DRIVER = True\\nexcept ImportError:  # pragma: no cover\\n    GraphDatabase = None\\n    Driver = None\\n    Session = None\\n    HAS_NEO4J_DRIVER = False\\n\\n# Setup structured logging\\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=\\\"%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(name)s: %(message)s\\\")\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\\\"law_enforcement_intel_api\\\")\\n\\n# =====================================================================\\n# Configuration & Environment\\n# =====================================================================\\n\\nNEO4J_URI: str = os.getenv(\\\"NEO4J_URI\\\", \\\"bolt://localhost:7687\\\")\\nNEO4J_USER: str = os.getenv(\\\"NEO4J_USER\\\", \\\"neo4j\\\")\\nNEO4J_PASSWORD: str = os.getenv(\\\"NEO4J_PASSWORD\\\", \\\"password123\\\")\\n\\n# Global Neo4j Driver instance\\n_neo4j_driver: Driver | None = None\\n\\n\\ndef get_driver() -> Driver | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Initialize or return the global Neo4j driver.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    global _neo4j_driver\\n    if _neo4j_driver is None and HAS_NEO4J_DRIVER and GraphDatabase is not None:\\n        try:\\n            _neo4j_driver = GraphDatabase.driver(\\n                NEO4J_URI,\\n                auth=(NEO4J_USER, NEO4J_PASSWORD),\\n                max_connection_lifetime=3600,\\n            )\\n            logger.info(\\\n<truncated 19987 bytes>","Description":"\"Create main.py in artifact scratch directory\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Nityam Jaiswal\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\de4af87e-228e-4ca7-8d2e-80c696fe372e\\\\scratch\\\\main.py\"","toolAction":"\"Create file\"","toolSummary":"\"Creating main.py in scratch\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
